# HakiOS fragment: the Qualcomm SM8250 family (Snapdragon 865 "kona"; the 865+ too) -- what is true of the SoC, whatever phone
# it is in. The processor has eight cores and the biggest is core 7: the OnePlus 8 Pro's tree gives cpu0-3 capacity 1024 (the
# Cortex-A55s at 1.8 GHz), cpu4-7 capacity 1894 (the Cortex-A77s), cpu7 the 2.84 GHz prime.
# The SoC-family drivers the SC7280 fragment turns on are written for that SoC's addresses and firmware; none is made to work
# on sm8250 yet, so this fragment turns no driver on: the port turns each on when its kona facts are written (what each needs:
# devices/oneplus8pro/README.md). Until then a device's own fragment leaves the phone drivers out as well.
CONFIG_SOC="sm8250"
CONFIG_CPUS=8
CONFIG_BOOTCPU=7

# the SC7280 fragment's four, off until their sm8250 port exists (their built-in defaults are the SC7280's addresses):
# CONFIG_CPUFREQ is not set      (kona: the apps RSC drv-2 at 0x18220000 is in soc.args; the APSS side is not written)
# CONFIG_SOCINFO is not set      (the SMEM item numbers of kona; soc_smem=0x80900000 is in soc.args)
# CONFIG_THERMAL is not set      (kona's TSENS is another generation; thermal_tm0/1 boot-args when the port comes)
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_CPUFREQ is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_SOCINFO is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_THERMAL is not set
# CONFIG_HAKIOS_PMIC is not set  (kona carries PM8150/PM8150B/PM8150L/PM8009, not the SC7280's PM8350)
